  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788664",
      "title": "Using localStorage for Data Storage",
      "lectureOrder": 63,
      "videoOrder": 59,
      "sourceHash": "e0734f869a739da9be75ce2ffcbce25614c7661314664a13f9fb75bf0000f50d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 3.54,
          "en": "So now that you also got an introduction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.54,
          "end": 7.02,
          "en": "to services and dependency injection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.02,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "you really have a solid foundation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 13.05,
          "en": "about all the core Angular essentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.05,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "every Angular developer needs to know.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 18.03,
          "en": "Before we conclude this module, though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.03,
          "end": 20.46,
          "en": "there's one last little enhancement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.46,
          "end": 22.59,
          "en": "that we could make to this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.59,
          "end": 23.85,
          "en": "because at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.85,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "it works such that all the changes we make,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 30.3,
          "en": "all the tasks we add or we mark as completed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 32.98,
          "en": "are lost whenever we reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.05,
          "end": 37.56,
          "en": "because we're only working with some dummy data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.56,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "that's stored in memory",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 43.323,
          "en": "and that's always recreated when the app restarts therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.31,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "And we could improve this app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 51.62,
          "en": "by storing at least the tasks in a more persistent storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.32,
          "end": 54.99,
          "en": "Now, later in the course, you will learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.99,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "how to connect your Angular application to a backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 60.72,
          "en": "so to a server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.72,
          "end": 64.2,
          "en": "where data could be stored in a real database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.2,
          "end": 65.73,
          "en": "But for the moment here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.73,
          "end": 68.85,
          "en": "I'll just store that data in the browser storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 71.07300000000001,
          "en": "which is better than nothing, I guess.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.24,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "So the idea is to fetch the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "from the browser storage when the app loads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 84.69,
          "en": "and to update the tasks stored in the browser storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.69,
          "end": 87.123,
          "en": "whenever we add or remove a task,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.08,
          "end": 90.9,
          "en": "and I'll start with the initialization.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.9,
          "end": 95.263,
          "en": "For that, we can add a constructor here to this TasksService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.43,
          "en": "because as you learned, that's a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 101.493,
          "en": "that's automatically executed when the app starts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.50999999999999,
          "end": 106.2,
          "en": "And in there, we could set this.tasks array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.2,
          "end": 111.2,
          "en": "equal to data that we fetch from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.69,
          "end": 115.22999999999999,
          "en": "Now, I'll actually do that with help of a helper constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.22999999999999,
          "end": 118.02000000000001,
          "en": "where I reach out to localStorage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.02000000000001,
          "end": 120.66,
          "en": "and where I then call getItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.66,
          "end": 123.39,
          "en": "to get some data from local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.39,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "which should be stored under a key of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 130.38,
          "en": "So the assumption is that in the browser's local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.38,
          "end": 134.13,
          "en": "we're storing some tasks with a key of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.13,
          "end": 137.7,
          "en": "Next, I wanna check if some tasks were found,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.7,
          "end": 140.07,
          "en": "and if I did find some tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 140.07,
          "end": 142.56,
          "en": "so if some data was stored there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.56,
          "end": 146.16,
          "en": "which will not be the case when we run this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 146.16,
          "end": 149.67000000000002,
          "en": "for the first time, but if we do have some tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 149.67000000000002,
          "end": 152.64,
          "en": "then I wanna overwrite my tasks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.64,
          "end": 154.953,
          "en": "with the tasks from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.09,
          "end": 159.32999999999998,
          "en": "However, the tasks we retrieve from local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.32999999999998,
          "end": 162.78,
          "en": "this constant here, will always be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 162.78,
          "end": 166.14,
          "en": "because we can't store complex values like arrays",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.14,
          "end": 168.9,
          "en": "or objects in local storage like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.9,
          "end": 172.14,
          "en": "Instead, we have to convert them to JSON first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 172.14,
          "end": 175.47,
          "en": "which in the end is a string that has a certain format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.47,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "So the assumption is that the tasks, if they exist,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 181.53,
          "en": "will be stored in that JSON format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.53,
          "end": 185.04,
          "en": "which is a standard format in programming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "And therefore, here, I'll actually parse the tasks as JSON",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 191.73,
          "en": "to convert them back to an array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 191.73,
          "end": 193.203,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 194.37,
          "end": 197.85,
          "en": "So I keep my dummy tasks if no tasks are found,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 197.85,
          "end": 201.32999999999998,
          "en": "but if tasks are found, I'll use those instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 201.32999999999998,
          "end": 202.653,
          "en": "That's the idea here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 203.91,
          "end": 206.46,
          "en": "Well, and now we need to update the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.46,
          "end": 209.013,
          "en": "whenever we save or remove a task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 212.73,
          "en": "And therefore, I'll add another helper method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.73,
          "end": 215.64,
          "en": "a private method, which is only meant to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.64,
          "end": 220.317,
          "en": "from inside this service class, which I'll name saveTasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.127,
          "end": 226.15699999999998,
          "en": "And here, I will simply call localStorage.setItem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.961,
          "end": 231.06,
          "en": "and set an item with a key of tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.06,
          "end": 234.51,
          "en": "because that's also the key we're looking for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 234.51,
          "end": 236.643,
          "en": "when retrieving the tasks here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.22,
          "end": 242.43,
          "en": "And I wanna store my tasks array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 242.43,
          "end": 247.43,
          "en": "So I will now use JSON.stringify to convert this.tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.97,
          "end": 252.69,
          "en": "the tasks array that's currently managed by this service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.69,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "to such a string in the JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "And that will then be stored in local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 263.01,
          "en": "And now we just have to call this.saveTasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 263.01,
          "end": 264.66,
          "en": "after removing a task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 264.66,
          "end": 267.933,
          "en": "and after adding a task in both places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 274.47,
          "en": "Well, and with that, if you now save that and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 274.47,
          "end": 277.77,
          "en": "you'll see the tasks are still there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 277.77,
          "end": 279.84000000000003,
          "en": "But if I now complete a task",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 279.84000000000003,
          "end": 282.6,
          "en": "and I therefore change my tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 282.6,
          "end": 286.11,
          "en": "you can see if you use the browser developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 290.58,
          "en": "and you go to the application tab that under local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 290.58,
          "end": 293.28,
          "en": "there is a tasks key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 293.28,
          "end": 295.75,
          "en": "and the value under that key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 296.67,
          "end": 301.67,
          "en": "is now actually this string with the tasks in this format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 302.67,
          "end": 304.02,
          "en": "It might not look like a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 304.02,
          "end": 306.543,
          "en": "but it is stored in a string in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 308.88,
          "end": 311.4,
          "en": "So the data is stored and therefore indeed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 311.4,
          "end": 314.55,
          "en": "if I reload, we can see that for Marcus here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 314.55,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "we only have one task now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 318.27,
          "en": "because we're now using the tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 318.27,
          "end": 320.313,
          "en": "that are loaded from local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 321.42,
          "end": 325.11,
          "en": "And this isn't an Angular-specific feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 325.11,
          "end": 326.49,
          "en": "or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 326.49,
          "end": 328.35,
          "en": "but I think it's a nice enhancement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.35,
          "end": 330.9,
          "en": "for this first demo app here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 330.9,
          "end": 332.85,
          "en": "which now allowed us to explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 332.85,
          "end": 335.73,
          "en": "all those crucial Angular essentials",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.73,
          "end": 338.373,
          "en": "every Angular developer must know.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
